1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,592
Their getaway car came back with a blue
door. Jason had paid for cream,

2
00:00:05,592 --> 00:00:07,190
and Lucia wanted answers.

3
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:11,976
The painter shrugged and pointed at the
invoice. One door replaced. Color

4
00:00:11,976 --> 00:00:13,970
matching had never been included.

5
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:18,763
Jason called it a mistake. Lucia called
it a landmark. Everyone they'd

6
00:00:18,763 --> 00:00:20,760
passed would remember this car.

7
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:25,154
Then the painter mentioned the owner
who'd collected his cream door

8
00:00:25,154 --> 00:00:27,950
yesterday, smiling through a mouthful of
excuses.

9
00:00:27,950 --> 00:00:31,943
Lucia opened their envelope. The
ownership papers were photocopies. Their

10
00:00:31,943 --> 00:00:33,940
car had been sold twice.

11
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:39,133
Jason looked at the keys. The engine
still worked. That made walking away

12
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:41,130
feel harder than it should.

13
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:47,113
They left the coupe with the shop and
filed their claim from the bus stop

14
00:00:47,113 --> 00:00:48,310
across the street.

15
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:53,864
The bus arrived blue and cream. Lucia
laughed first. This time, Jason knew

16
00:00:53,864 --> 00:00:56,000
exactly what their fare bought.
